---
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import CodeBlock from '../../components/CodeBlock.astro';
---

<DocsLayout title="Server Guide">
  <h1>Server Guide</h1>
  <p>
    The hostedat server is a single binary that handles everything: serving static sites, managing users,
    handling HTTPS, and exposing the API. No reverse proxy, no Docker, no external dependencies.
  </p>

  <h2>Quick start</h2>
  <p>Download the server binary for your platform from the <a href="/downloads">downloads page</a>, create a config file, and run it:</p>

  <CodeBlock
    code={`# Download the server binary
curl -fsSL https://docs.hostedat.ditto.moe/downloads/hostedat-server-linux-amd64 -o hostedat-server
chmod +x hostedat-server

# Create config
cp config.example.yaml config.yaml
# Edit config.yaml with your settings

# Run
./hostedat-server`}
    lang="bash"
  />

  <h2>First-run setup</h2>
  <p>
    On first launch with an empty database, the <strong>first user to register</strong> becomes the
    <strong>superadmin</strong>. This account has full control and cannot be demoted.
  </p>
  <ol>
    <li>Start the server</li>
    <li>Open the web UI at your configured domain</li>
    <li>Register the first account — this is your superadmin</li>
    <li>Configure registration settings (open, invite-only, or closed)</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>HTTPS & certificates</h2>
  <p>
    hostedat uses <strong>CertMagic</strong> (the ACME library from Caddy) to automatically obtain and renew
    wildcard TLS certificates from Let's Encrypt. This requires DNS-01 validation via Cloudflare.
  </p>

  <CodeBlock
    title="config.yaml"
    code={`# Listen on :443 for production HTTPS
listen: ":443"

# Cloudflare API token with Zone:DNS:Edit permission
cloudflare:
  api_token: "your-cloudflare-api-token"`}
    lang="yaml"
  />

  <p>
    The server will automatically obtain a wildcard cert for <code>*.yourdomain.com</code> and renew it
    before expiration. No cron jobs, no manual renewal.
  </p>

  <h3>Development mode (no TLS)</h3>
  <p>For local development, listen on a non-443 port and leave the Cloudflare token empty:</p>
  <CodeBlock
    title="config.yaml"
    code={`listen: ":8080"
cloudflare:
  api_token: ""`}
    lang="yaml"
  />

  <h2>Database</h2>
  <p>
    hostedat uses <strong>GORM</strong> with SQLite by default. The database file is created automatically.
    For production, you can switch to PostgreSQL or MySQL by changing the driver and DSN:
  </p>
  <CodeBlock
    title="config.yaml"
    code={`# SQLite (default)
database:
  driver: sqlite
  dsn: ./data/hostedat.db

# PostgreSQL
database:
  driver: postgres
  dsn: "host=localhost port=5432 user=hostedat dbname=hostedat sslmode=disable"

# MySQL
database:
  driver: mysql
  dsn: "hostedat:password@tcp(localhost:3306)/hostedat?parseTime=true"`}
    lang="yaml"
  />

  <h2>Static site features</h2>
  <p>hostedat supports several features that make it compatible with sites built for Netlify or Cloudflare Pages.</p>

  <h3>_redirects file</h3>
  <p>Place a <code>_redirects</code> file in the root of your uploaded site to define redirect and rewrite rules:</p>
  <CodeBlock
    title="_redirects"
    code={`# Redirects (browser URL changes)
/old-path    /new-path    301
/blog/*      /new-blog/:splat 302

# Rewrites (transparent, URL stays the same)
/api/*       https://api.example.com/:splat 200

# SPA fallback (must be last)
/*           /index.html  200`}
    lang="text"
  />

  <ul>
    <li><code>301</code> / <code>302</code> — redirect (browser URL changes)</li>
    <li><code>200</code> — rewrite (serve target content at original URL)</li>
    <li><code>*</code> wildcard is captured and available as <code>:splat</code></li>
    <li>First match wins, evaluated top-to-bottom</li>
    <li>Static files always take precedence over rules</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>_headers file</h3>
  <p>Custom response headers for matching paths:</p>
  <CodeBlock
    title="_headers"
    code={`/*
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff

/*.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable`}
    lang="text"
  />

  <h3>Custom 404</h3>
  <p>Include a <code>404.html</code> file in your upload to show a custom 404 page when no file matches.</p>

  <h3>SPA mode</h3>
  <p>
    Toggle SPA mode per-site via the dashboard or API. When enabled, all unmatched routes
    serve <code>index.html</code> — equivalent to having <code>/* /index.html 200</code> as the last
    <code>_redirects</code> rule.
  </p>

  <h2>User roles</h2>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Role</th><th>Capabilities</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>superadmin</strong></td>
        <td>Full control. First registered user. Cannot be demoted.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>admin</strong></td>
        <td>Manage users, sites, invites. Can be promoted/demoted by superadmin.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>user</strong></td>
        <td>Create sites, deploy, manage own API keys.</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Running as a service</h2>
  <p>For production, run hostedat as a systemd service:</p>
  <CodeBlock
    title="/etc/systemd/system/hostedat.service"
    code={`[Unit]
Description=hostedat static site hosting
After=network.target

[Service]
Type=simple
User=hostedat
WorkingDirectory=/opt/hostedat
ExecStart=/opt/hostedat/hostedat-server
Restart=always
RestartSec=5

[Install]
WantedBy=multi-user.target`}
    lang="ini"
  />

  <CodeBlock
    code={`sudo systemctl enable hostedat
sudo systemctl start hostedat`}
    lang="bash"
  />

  <hr />
  <p>Next: <a href="/docs/configuration">Configuration Reference</a> for all config options.</p>
</DocsLayout>
